+# Password Hashing
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use Argon2id as the password hashing algorithm. It was chosen because it is memory-hard and time-hard, which makes it resistant to GPU-accelerated brute-force attacks and raises the cost of exploiting a credential compromise. No parameter values (memory, iterations, parallelism) are recorded in the project's decisions.
